WEBVTT

00:12.561 --> 00:14.312
I'm uh... gonna go buy a drink.

00:14.396 --> 00:15.480
Wait, Amamiya.

00:15.564 --> 00:16.690
I'm coming too.

00:24.823 --> 00:25.991
Without a word...

00:26.575 --> 00:27.909
We've arrived...

00:36.918 --> 00:38.170
[REACTION}

00:38.712 --> 00:39.588
Hey, hey,

00:39.671 --> 00:43.091
When they come back to the classroom
from getting their drinks, what do you

00:43.175 --> 00:45.302
think they'd do if we suddenly
weren't here?

00:45.385 --> 00:47.512
THE TWO HAVE COMPLETELY LOST FOCUS

00:47.596 --> 00:48.430
Should we?

00:50.432 --> 00:51.391
THUMP, THUMP, THUMP

00:51.475 --> 00:52.309
So hot.

00:53.018 --> 00:54.102
- Minato!
- So cold.

00:54.186 --> 00:55.771
Mm? Oh.

00:55.854 --> 00:57.397
Hey, how's it going Kenta!

00:57.481 --> 00:59.441
You studying the past exams I gave you?

01:01.276 --> 01:02.235
It's a senior.

01:03.278 --> 01:05.447
- Scurry, scurry, scurry.
- I was studying them, but I just

01:05.530 --> 01:07.407
- took a break.
- Is that really true?

01:08.784 --> 01:10.827
- An underclassman?
- Yeah. Ain't he cute?

01:11.328 --> 01:13.205
Is Kenta being a good senior to you?

01:13.705 --> 01:17.167
He's always acting like he's hot
stuff, but he's mostly just trouble.

01:17.250 --> 01:19.336
- Fade...
- What're you saying?

01:20.545 --> 01:22.214
- See ya.
- Later.

01:22.297 --> 01:23.715
- Bye.
- Later!

01:24.216 --> 01:25.634
Are you done talking?

01:25.717 --> 01:26.760
HIkawa.

01:27.511 --> 01:30.514
You know you didn't have to lie low just
because of them.

01:30.597 --> 01:33.642
Oh, it's more like I was kinda
just hiding because they were

01:33.725 --> 01:35.352
upperclassmen I didn't know.

01:35.852 --> 01:37.437
Were you afraid?

01:38.271 --> 01:39.689
MEMORIES OF JUNIOR HIGH

01:39.773 --> 01:40.690
- Kinda.
- Mmm.

01:40.774 --> 01:42.109
Shy around new people.

01:42.734 --> 01:43.568
Oh.

01:48.657 --> 01:50.534
- Hey, Hikawa
- Uh-huh?

01:51.034 --> 01:53.870
Then are you afraid of me?

01:54.663 --> 01:55.497
Huh?

01:58.041 --> 01:59.835
- Mm-mm.
- Not anymore.

02:00.544 --> 02:01.503
No, absolutely not.

02:08.718 --> 02:10.554
Man, I'm so glad.

02:13.807 --> 02:16.184
- Huh?
- That's right.

02:16.685 --> 02:20.689
Amamiya's human just like me, and gets
hurt and worries about things, too

02:21.898 --> 02:23.900
I mean that should be obvious but...

02:25.569 --> 02:28.572
How had I been acting toward him
this whole time?

02:32.075 --> 02:32.909
Hey, Amamiya.

02:33.410 --> 02:34.452
What do I do?

02:34.536 --> 02:36.371
I can't look her in the eye.

02:37.831 --> 02:39.916
- [REACTION}
- [REACTION}

02:40.000 --> 02:41.001
Huh?

02:43.420 --> 02:44.254
Co-! Co-!

02:45.589 --> 02:47.632
- Co?
- Cockroach! There's a cockroach!

02:47.716 --> 02:48.842
- Whoa!
- Ah! See?!

02:49.968 --> 02:51.678
- There! There!
- Huh? Wait, what?

02:52.179 --> 02:53.013
Ugh!

02:55.223 --> 02:56.057
Uh...

02:56.933 --> 02:57.767
Uh...

02:58.685 --> 02:59.519
- Uh.
- Uh.

03:00.020 --> 03:00.854
GIGGLE

03:00.937 --> 03:01.813
CHUCKLE

03:03.773 --> 03:04.608
I can't!

03:07.027 --> 03:08.612
You were losing your mind!

03:08.695 --> 03:09.738
I was.

03:10.655 --> 03:11.489
Sorry.

03:12.949 --> 03:16.286
I don't wanna get close to her by forcing
my way through the door.

03:17.037 --> 03:19.873
I wanna do it the right way, and
be friends.

03:20.707 --> 03:21.750
And see her smile.

03:23.001 --> 03:23.835
That's all.

03:26.087 --> 03:27.547
That's all I want.

03:28.465 --> 03:29.466
And yet...

05:01.933 --> 05:05.729
Self-awareness

05:06.771 --> 05:08.523
Well, those two aren't coming back.

05:10.692 --> 05:13.486
Don't you think they're taking way
too long of a break? Do they even plan

05:13.570 --> 05:15.613
to study? We have exams!

05:15.697 --> 05:17.449
That doesn't sound like you at all.

05:18.158 --> 05:21.995
EXECUTING THE "WILL THEY BE SURPRISED
IF NO ONE'S HERE WHEN THEY COME BACK?"

05:23.830 --> 05:24.914
Do you like anyone?

05:26.958 --> 05:28.251
Wh- why do you wanna know?

05:28.335 --> 05:32.756
Well, I never hear stuff like that about
you, so I couldn't help but be curious.

05:38.803 --> 05:39.637
Miki.

05:46.895 --> 05:47.729
Koyun...

05:48.355 --> 05:49.189
Huh?

05:49.272 --> 05:51.191
Hayato, Daichi, and Gin.

05:51.691 --> 05:53.860
Dad, Mom, Haruto, Sakura...

05:54.361 --> 05:56.446
Wait, wait, wait. You're missing someone.

05:56.529 --> 05:58.198
Why aren't you mentioning Minato?

06:02.035 --> 06:03.203
Well, Yota.

06:03.703 --> 06:07.624
If you ever do find someone you like,
I just want you to know that you have my

06:07.707 --> 06:08.875
full support.

06:09.376 --> 06:11.920
After all, you've done so much for me.

06:17.842 --> 06:19.803
- You're such a good friend!
- Yay!

06:22.097 --> 06:23.139
Oh, they're back!

06:25.100 --> 06:26.351
Huh? They're gone.

06:26.434 --> 06:27.936
Their bags are still here.

06:28.019 --> 06:29.104
Bathroom break?

06:31.272 --> 06:33.149
Well, they'll be back eventually.

06:33.650 --> 06:34.984
I guess you're right.

06:38.321 --> 06:41.950
The way Yota hides his feelings for her,
while trying to stay friends with

06:42.033 --> 06:43.493
her and pretending it's fine...

06:44.077 --> 06:46.496
You can tell he's working hard
to shove it down.

06:47.372 --> 06:51.209
On that note, if Hikawa were to fall for
Yota, then her feelings wouldn't be

06:51.292 --> 06:52.919
reciprocated.

06:54.754 --> 06:56.047
She shouldn't go there.

06:57.257 --> 06:58.508
Or that's what I thought.

06:59.884 --> 07:01.428
But easier said than done.

07:01.511 --> 07:04.431
That's not something you can just turn on
and off at will.

07:06.015 --> 07:06.850
Ahhh...

07:07.600 --> 07:09.519
I wish I hadn't noticed.

07:10.562 --> 07:13.148
I feel like she finally opened her
heart up to me a little, but now...

07:13.231 --> 07:16.234
I have to be more careful moving forward.

07:16.317 --> 07:17.152
Amamiya.

07:20.989 --> 07:23.700
Here you go. I only had two of them left.

07:23.783 --> 07:25.201
So I want you to have one.

07:27.454 --> 07:29.205
Uh. Th-Thanks.

07:31.749 --> 07:33.710
Ahhh. I really hate this.

07:34.794 --> 07:37.130
You weren't gonna share the candy
with us, huh?

07:37.213 --> 07:38.047
You were there?

07:43.219 --> 07:45.513
ART ROOM

07:45.597 --> 07:48.141
Hey, Tsukiko, have you always eaten
in the art room?

07:48.224 --> 07:49.058
Yeah.

07:49.142 --> 07:50.268
This way I can eat quickly and
then continue working during

07:50.351 --> 07:51.186
my lunch break.

07:52.854 --> 07:55.064
- How practical.
- Remember me?

07:55.148 --> 07:56.232
From episode six!

07:56.316 --> 07:57.775
Tsukiko Shimojima.

07:58.568 --> 08:02.572
So towards the beginning, I started out
by eating with everyone in the classroom

08:03.072 --> 08:04.991
But our group was pretty big.

08:09.162 --> 08:13.082
But there was this kind of unspoken rule
that no one would start eating 'til

08:13.166 --> 08:15.376
everyone was there.

08:16.127 --> 08:18.505
I started to think, "Wait, hold on,
this isn't right."

08:18.588 --> 08:20.423
"This doesn't mean being close."

08:20.507 --> 08:24.177
Then I just started to slowly distance
myself, and broke away from them.

08:24.260 --> 08:25.553
HA HA...

08:26.054 --> 08:27.180
Ah!

08:27.847 --> 08:30.767
Oh, but just to be clear, I'm not on bad
terms with anyone.

08:30.850 --> 08:33.394
I hang out with them separately,
even now, and...

08:33.478 --> 08:37.232
Oh no! I just told her something that
reveals how terrible I am! Ahhh!

08:37.315 --> 08:38.775
- I get it.
- Huh?

08:38.858 --> 08:41.402
In fact I get it so much I feel sick.

08:42.070 --> 08:45.073
- Empathy.
- Um. A- Are you okay?

08:45.698 --> 08:48.952
You see, I'm not good in group settings
either.

08:49.536 --> 08:51.204
To be honest, I can totally tell.

08:54.457 --> 08:55.291
Hmm.

08:55.959 --> 08:56.960
Oh, man.

08:57.460 --> 09:00.838
You know, I really wish you and I had
started talking way sooner.

09:07.220 --> 09:08.054
- What?
- Oh!

09:08.137 --> 09:10.098
GRADE 1 CLASS 6 AFTER SCHOOL STUDY TIME

09:13.935 --> 09:15.186
Are you in the mood... Hey.

09:15.937 --> 09:17.105
For some curry?

09:17.689 --> 09:18.523
- Huh?
- Huh?

09:18.606 --> 09:20.400
- Huh?
- Do you ever not want curry?

09:20.483 --> 09:21.526
Come on.

09:21.609 --> 09:23.778
Oh. You're going along with this. Good.

09:24.279 --> 09:27.699
Apparently, there's a famous curry
place in the new mall that opened

09:34.038 --> 09:36.291
- I don't mind.
- Me neither.

09:36.374 --> 09:37.875
What about your family dinner?

09:38.376 --> 09:40.837
Koyun, you always seem to be
worried about that.

09:40.920 --> 09:41.879
It's alright.

09:41.963 --> 09:42.797
Uh, "Always?"

09:43.423 --> 09:45.466
Yes! Alright!

09:45.550 --> 09:46.676
Let's go!

09:47.302 --> 09:50.597
- Trot, trot, trot, trot, trot, trot, trot,
- Trot, trot, trot, trot, trot, trot, trot,

09:50.680 --> 09:51.514
Wow.

09:52.098 --> 09:54.183
Yota, you're able to hold onto that part?

09:54.267 --> 09:55.101
What?

09:55.184 --> 09:56.019
SPARKLE, SPARKLE

09:56.102 --> 09:57.520
- That's so nice.
- Is it?

09:57.604 --> 09:59.606
I can stand without holding anything.

10:00.273 --> 10:01.107
Core strength!

10:01.190 --> 10:02.692
Why's it a competition?

10:06.070 --> 10:08.156
- You're heavy.
- Hold yourself up!

10:08.781 --> 10:10.575
I'm not using my hands so it counts.

10:10.658 --> 10:11.743
That's so cheating.

10:25.715 --> 10:29.594
It wasn't all that long ago... that things
were so different.

10:32.930 --> 10:36.267
In junior high, it's like I was
living in a fish tank, despite not

10:36.351 --> 10:38.561
being able to breathe underwater.

10:39.812 --> 10:42.815
Being different from everyone else was
total agony for me.

10:43.858 --> 10:46.152
I decided it wasn't where I belonged.

10:47.111 --> 10:49.697
But then I found out I didn't belong
anywhere.

10:50.657 --> 10:53.534
I was ashamed I couldn't seem to
figure out how to adapt.

10:54.202 --> 10:55.036
It hurt.

10:55.536 --> 10:56.371
A lot.

10:57.705 --> 10:58.539
But...

11:00.375 --> 11:03.795
Once I was able to get out of the
fish tank, I realized that none of

11:03.878 --> 11:06.589
it actually had to be that painful.

11:07.382 --> 11:10.968
I just needed to break free from that
small world I had been living in.

11:12.053 --> 11:14.013
Everything just seemed so trivial then.

11:18.059 --> 11:20.937
Club activities, school events and even
friendships.

11:21.938 --> 11:25.400
If I could get through high school
in peace, I felt like nothing else

11:25.483 --> 11:26.442
mattered.

11:31.364 --> 11:33.282
The world around me has changed, but...

11:34.826 --> 11:35.660
Wow!

11:35.743 --> 11:38.746
The area around here has become so nice,
hasn't it?

11:38.830 --> 11:41.249
Can I say that I myself have really
changed?

11:42.792 --> 11:45.044
So much has changed since they
built the mall.

11:45.128 --> 11:47.338
I bet the rent around here has gone up
like crazy.

11:47.422 --> 11:48.297
Why do you care?

11:49.132 --> 11:51.134
Yeah. It'll be okay.

11:51.926 --> 11:53.469
Those bad memories...

11:54.053 --> 11:55.805
I can act like they never happened.

11:56.681 --> 12:00.685
GRAND OPENING SALE NOW IN PROGRESS

12:01.728 --> 12:02.562
Okay.

12:03.229 --> 12:06.649
We're right here and the food court
is here, so this way.

12:07.191 --> 12:08.317
POWER WALKING

12:08.401 --> 12:09.402
Gah! Uh!

12:11.738 --> 12:13.698
- Happen. It's the opposite direction.
- Hm?

12:13.781 --> 12:14.782
Here, this way.

12:15.491 --> 12:17.452
Really? This isn't a trick?

12:17.535 --> 12:18.619
I promise you.

12:19.454 --> 12:21.873
What was that whole, "I know you so well"
thing?

12:29.839 --> 12:30.673
- Hm?
- Seriously?

12:30.757 --> 12:31.591
Yep!

12:34.719 --> 12:35.553
Huh?

12:36.345 --> 12:38.097
- Miki!
- What?! What do you want?

12:38.598 --> 12:39.891
Igarashi is here.

12:42.351 --> 12:44.353
We're actually not on very good terms.

12:44.937 --> 12:47.607
He and Hikawa really shouldn't see each
other, right?

12:49.525 --> 12:51.027
I'm assuming Koyun told you?

12:51.861 --> 12:53.029
That they dated.

12:53.529 --> 12:54.489
Yeah...

12:54.572 --> 12:55.698
She told me a little.

12:56.199 --> 12:57.867
Like they're on bad terms.

12:58.409 --> 13:00.745
If they ran into each other, would they
fight?

13:01.454 --> 13:04.040
No, I don't think it would go that far,
but...

13:04.123 --> 13:07.627
Well, if it's going to upset Hikawa,
then we don't want them seeing

13:07.710 --> 13:08.628
each other.

13:09.170 --> 13:10.213
Mm-hm, agreed.

13:10.713 --> 13:11.547
Hm?

13:16.594 --> 13:17.637
What's wrong, Koyun?

13:18.721 --> 13:19.722
I can't let him see!

13:20.306 --> 13:22.016
- Yota, look! A dog over there! Let's go
- Huh?

13:22.099 --> 13:23.309
- See it!
- Uh, wait, what?

13:23.392 --> 13:25.812
I mean, who knows, maybe nothing will
happen either.

13:25.895 --> 13:28.981
It's possible he may have just moved
past it by now anyway.

13:29.690 --> 13:31.901
Oh... That's possible.

13:32.527 --> 13:33.402
Hikawa?

13:34.278 --> 13:37.031
No, there was no one by that name in our
junior high.

13:39.575 --> 13:42.954
But still, I don't know how you could
forget someone's existence.

13:43.704 --> 13:47.041
Well, there shouldn't be an issue if
things are going well with his new

13:47.124 --> 13:48.417
girlfriend, right?.

13:48.501 --> 13:49.544
Huh?

13:50.211 --> 13:51.462
Oh. Never mind.

13:51.546 --> 13:52.505
Thinking out loud here.

13:52.588 --> 13:56.050
I don't know anything about his love life
after starting high school.

13:56.843 --> 13:59.762
Maybe he doesn't even have one. But it
seems like he would, right? I have no

13:59.846 --> 14:01.222
- idea, though.
- Girlfriend?

14:02.598 --> 14:03.432
Huh?

14:05.810 --> 14:08.187
- Thank you for the meal.
- Thank you for the meal.

14:08.271 --> 14:10.857
- Hey, hey, hey! Get out of my way!
- So loud!

14:11.357 --> 14:12.733
PLAYER FOUR - PLAYER THREE

14:12.817 --> 14:13.651
Huh.

14:13.734 --> 14:17.154
- I'll be damned if I allow anybody to race
- Oh man, someone's using it right now.

14:17.238 --> 14:18.155
Ahead of me! Over my dead body,
you hear me?

14:18.239 --> 14:19.448
We'll go somewhere else.

14:20.074 --> 14:23.619
ONDO MASTER

14:23.703 --> 14:24.537
- Wah!
- Oh!

14:24.620 --> 14:27.999
UPPI PRINT STICKER

14:28.082 --> 14:29.333
Do it! Why can't you?

14:29.417 --> 14:32.420
- We're here, so we might as well just
- Uhhh, are you sure I can go in here?

14:32.503 --> 14:33.337
I get nervous.

14:33.421 --> 14:34.797
Let's go! Three, two, one!

14:34.881 --> 14:35.715
Yay!

14:37.300 --> 14:40.261
I ended up having a really good time in
spite of myself.

14:40.344 --> 14:42.555
Goofing off before exams feels
incredible.

14:43.055 --> 14:44.515
I could get used to this.

14:44.599 --> 14:46.183
Well, don't make a habit of it.

14:46.893 --> 14:48.477
We'll study some more tomorrow.

14:49.979 --> 14:50.813
Yota!

14:52.732 --> 14:53.608
See ya!

14:54.400 --> 14:55.568
- See you later.
- Later.

15:03.618 --> 15:04.452
Nicely done.

15:05.036 --> 15:05.870
Huh?

15:05.953 --> 15:06.787
For what?

15:09.874 --> 15:14.128
There shouldn't be an issue if things are
going well with his new girlfriend right?

15:14.211 --> 15:16.964
I mean of course she's had past romantic
relationships.

15:17.840 --> 15:20.092
But it still took me by surprise.

15:20.176 --> 15:21.594
And with Igarashi?

15:23.179 --> 15:27.099
I mean, when I look at it objectively,
it at least kind of makes sense how she

15:27.183 --> 15:29.226
might have feelings for Yota, but...

15:29.810 --> 15:31.562
No, don't think about that!

15:34.357 --> 15:35.608
Ohhh, man.

15:37.944 --> 15:39.820
I just don't get it.

15:44.367 --> 15:46.077
Yep, vators are the best!

15:46.911 --> 15:50.748
The only person who'd call an elevator a
"vator", would be you Mi- ki...

15:51.666 --> 15:52.500
Huh?

15:59.632 --> 16:00.883
In junior high...

16:02.301 --> 16:04.095
I hated Tsubasa Igarashi.

16:05.054 --> 16:08.182
- That doesn't look very interesting.
- Mismatched personalities.

16:08.265 --> 16:10.101
- A one-sided affection.
- I'm serious!

16:10.184 --> 16:11.811
Come on, you've got Igarashi, right?

16:11.894 --> 16:14.188
Even those on the sidelines involving
themselves in my life.

16:14.271 --> 16:15.439
Yuishira, don't keep Igarashi waiting too
long.

16:15.523 --> 16:16.857
I hated it.

16:16.941 --> 16:17.900
I hated everything.

16:19.694 --> 16:23.197
But none of that's why I've been avoiding
him or even discussing him.

16:24.699 --> 16:27.284
This is a problem within myself.

16:30.454 --> 16:31.414
Oh, it's you.

16:31.998 --> 16:32.832
Huh?

16:34.500 --> 16:35.751
What's with that hair?

16:36.502 --> 16:37.336
GASP

16:37.420 --> 16:38.879
What about my hair? Huh?

16:38.963 --> 16:41.424
It was pretty weird the last time I saw
you, too

16:41.507 --> 16:45.136
What? I- It doesn't matter either way.
I look good in anything, no matter

16:45.219 --> 16:49.098
MATCHING HIS ENERGY FOR THE TIME BEING
MATCHING HIS ENERGY FOR THE TIME BEING

16:49.181 --> 16:51.308
I'm being treated as if I'm not
even here.

16:52.476 --> 16:55.980
After jumping out of the fish tank, the
more I get to know myself, the

16:56.063 --> 16:57.940
more I hate it.

17:02.528 --> 17:03.362
I...

17:04.363 --> 17:07.575
I never, ever had any feelings for you.

17:08.492 --> 17:12.288
I avoided him because I was scared
to face the person I hurt so maliciously.

17:12.371 --> 17:13.581
That's all.

17:14.415 --> 17:15.708
I'm just a coward.

17:18.294 --> 17:19.128
Well, see ya.

17:24.550 --> 17:25.426
Igarashi!

17:31.015 --> 17:31.891
What do you want?

17:32.433 --> 17:33.267
Uh.

17:33.851 --> 17:36.103
Has high school... been fun?

17:38.022 --> 17:40.066
Huh? What are you?

17:40.149 --> 17:42.443
My weird old aunt or something?

17:42.526 --> 17:45.529
BONG

17:45.613 --> 17:46.447
Wait.

17:46.530 --> 17:47.364
What do I do?

17:47.448 --> 17:49.533
As expected the conversation
doesn't flow.

17:49.617 --> 17:50.701
It's going fine.

17:50.785 --> 17:51.619
Huh?

17:52.161 --> 17:54.663
I mean, not like I need your concern or
anything.

18:00.795 --> 18:06.008
You know, when you stopped Igarashi
back there, man, I was totally surprised.

18:06.592 --> 18:07.593
Oh, thank you.

18:08.803 --> 18:09.637
I dunno.

18:09.720 --> 18:12.807
Maybe it's because hanging out
with you guys was so much fun.

18:13.808 --> 18:17.103
That could be why I acted so outta the
norm.

18:17.770 --> 18:18.604
Koyun.

18:26.153 --> 18:27.822
Here, thanks for this.

18:28.531 --> 18:30.491
Huh? What's with the lame bag?

18:30.991 --> 18:32.451
What, who cares what it looks like?

18:32.535 --> 18:33.410
You're just going home.

18:33.494 --> 18:35.996
It's not like you're gonna meet anyone on
the way.

18:37.498 --> 18:38.582
But I did meet someone.

18:38.666 --> 18:40.126
And of all people...

18:40.668 --> 18:42.419
Has high school... been fun?

18:43.420 --> 18:44.880
That's rich coming from you.

18:47.633 --> 18:48.467
Pain in the ass.

18:52.763 --> 18:53.597
Hey, so...

18:54.348 --> 18:57.393
It's my fault that you dated Igarashi,
isn't it?

18:58.310 --> 18:59.145
Sorry.

18:59.228 --> 19:01.981
It's because I wasn't considerate of
your feelings and said things I

19:02.064 --> 19:02.898
should've have.

19:04.942 --> 19:07.069
- Huh?
- Huh?

19:07.611 --> 19:09.655
Huh? What shouldn't you have said?

19:09.738 --> 19:10.906
Hold on, wait.

19:10.990 --> 19:14.410
Don't you remember what I told you
when we chatted here awhile back.

19:14.493 --> 19:16.996
How you should be glad to be liked and
not be greedy?

19:17.079 --> 19:19.582
Now that you mention it, I guess
you might have.

19:19.665 --> 19:21.375
What?! Wait, that's it?

19:21.876 --> 19:24.211
Sorry to disappoint, my memory's
a bit fuzzy.

19:24.295 --> 19:25.379
CONFUSION

19:25.462 --> 19:27.923
What?!
Wait, then why did you date Igarashi?

19:28.424 --> 19:29.466
Hmm.

19:32.052 --> 19:33.220
- That's secret.
- What?!

19:33.304 --> 19:34.138
DEVASTATED

19:34.221 --> 19:36.557
Because if I told you, you'd think
less of me.

19:38.559 --> 19:39.393
Wait a minute.

19:40.019 --> 19:40.853
Huh?

19:41.478 --> 19:43.981
- I'm not just gonna let that
- I'm not just gonna let that comment

19:44.064 --> 19:45.316
- comment slide.
- slide.

19:46.609 --> 19:47.443
Well, I...

19:48.903 --> 19:52.489
I thought I'd feel better about myself if
maybe I could fall for someone...

19:52.573 --> 19:54.158
Someone who loves me back.

19:55.451 --> 19:58.704
But instead of feeling better, I was just
in pain the whole time.

19:59.496 --> 20:01.290
And I ended up hurting Igarashi.

20:02.875 --> 20:04.919
Or I went out of my way to.

20:06.420 --> 20:08.505
My actions weren't lining up with my
heart.

20:08.589 --> 20:10.799
And I was really only thinking of myself.

20:11.717 --> 20:13.510
You can't stand people like that.

20:14.011 --> 20:14.887
Isn't that right?

20:17.473 --> 20:18.599
I can't say anything.

20:19.433 --> 20:23.145
Mm, because, no matter which path
you chose, Igarashi would've gotten hurt

20:23.229 --> 20:24.396
either way, right?

20:24.480 --> 20:27.274
So, really, I don't think that's
your fault, is it?

20:27.816 --> 20:31.153
And also, I couldn't possibly start
hating you out of the blue after

20:31.237 --> 20:32.613
all these years of friendship

20:32.696 --> 20:35.157
Besides, that's a dumb reason to hate
someone.

20:35.241 --> 20:36.533
BASHFUL...

20:36.617 --> 20:38.535
Uh! All right!

20:38.619 --> 20:41.497
Let's erase the past by having
awesome love lives now!

20:41.997 --> 20:44.083
What? That's okay, I don't really...

20:44.166 --> 20:47.670
- You can go date for both of us.
- I wonder what kind of guy he'll be.

20:47.753 --> 20:48.963
Huh?

20:49.880 --> 20:51.048
- Hmm.
- Okay, let's see.

20:51.757 --> 20:54.677
Obviously you should be with
someone who's the complete opposite of

20:54.760 --> 20:55.594
Igarashi.

20:55.678 --> 20:58.806
Someone who's kind but maybe
scatterbrained in a cute way.

20:58.889 --> 21:02.726
You should be with someone who embraces
everything you are, the way you are.

21:02.810 --> 21:05.771
Someone who's extremely accepting and
kind to other people.

21:07.648 --> 21:08.482
Hold on, this is about you, not me.

21:08.565 --> 21:09.400
WE SYNCHRONIZED...

21:09.483 --> 21:11.777
Hold on, this is about you, not me.

21:14.738 --> 21:17.908
Well, romantic relationships aren't
everything, right?

21:17.992 --> 21:21.954
And I'm having fun right now, but if we
had boyfriends, it would add more color

21:22.037 --> 21:23.205
to our lives!

21:23.956 --> 21:25.624
Like the tomatoes in a bento box.

21:27.418 --> 21:29.003
What kind of metaphor is that?

21:29.086 --> 21:30.087
Yeah, I dunno.

21:31.422 --> 21:32.256
Romance...

21:32.798 --> 21:35.509
Tell me the truth Koyuki, are you
really into Igarashi?

21:35.592 --> 21:36.760
ATAGAWA

21:38.262 --> 21:39.221
It's not like that.

21:39.930 --> 21:41.807
They're all just repeating the rumor.

21:42.641 --> 21:43.475
What?

21:45.978 --> 21:46.812
So you know...

21:46.895 --> 21:49.481
Atagawa's been coming on to me
super strong lately.

21:51.442 --> 21:54.153
Although, I'm not into in anyone but
the girl I like.

21:54.695 --> 21:56.405
She's barking up the wrong tree.

22:04.455 --> 22:05.289
You know, Miki...

22:06.540 --> 22:09.543
The harsh truth is I just don't have
a pure heart like you do.

22:09.626 --> 22:10.586
See ya!

22:10.669 --> 22:12.296
I'll be waiting for your tomato report!

22:12.379 --> 22:14.798
- If I'm honest, I really don't think...
- Ha! "Tomato report"!

22:14.882 --> 22:16.592
I should inflict myself on anyone.

22:18.260 --> 22:19.094
And so...

22:22.848 --> 22:24.641
I hope you go find happiness, Miki.
